# Suspending a card is a special action taken any time its owner could begin to cast it from their hand (CR 702.62a,
# 116.2f), so a permission to cast it as though it had flash lets it be suspended at instant speed (CR 601.3b, 702.8a).
# Valley Floodcaller lets Bot1 cast noncreature spells as though they had flash: in Bot2's turn Bot1 suspends Lotus Bloom,
# an artifact, which goes to exile. Without the Floodcaller the same suspend is refused out of
# timing (lotus-bloom-cannot-be-cast-or-suspended-out-of-timing).

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Valley Floodcaller
Lotus Bloom
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Valley Floodcaller.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Lotus Bloom.Suspend
? Turn = 2
? Exile = Lotus Bloom

[Expect]
Exile = Lotus Bloom
